# Genus does not drop under algebraically closed constant field extension

Theorem statement: `AlgebraicCurve.le_genusFF_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`
(`0043cc0f-67ac-50b2-bda5-7a7c57d37045`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `00e0f2cd-fd91-5a4d-a67a-e1414a431576`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K \subseteq K' \subseteq F'$ and $K \subseteq F \subseteq F'$ be fields with compatible algebra
structures (two scalar towers $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$), with $K$ and $K'$
algebraically closed. Assume that $F$ is a one-variable function field over $K$ in the explicit
sense that there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over $K(x)$, and
likewise that there is $x' \in F'$ transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite-dimensional over
$K'(x')$. Assume further `IsCurveOver K F` and `IsCurveOver K' F'`, i.e. for each of the two
extensions: every nonzero $f$ admits a divisor $D$ with $D(v) = v(\operatorname{ord} f)$ at all
places $v$ and $\deg D = 0$ (places being valuation subrings of the function field that contain the
constants, are not the whole field, and are principal ideal rings), every place has residue field
finite-dimensional over the constant field, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank
one over the function field. Finally assume $F'$ is generated as a field over $K'$ by the image of
$F$, i.e. the $K'$-subfield of $F'$ generated by $\operatorname{range}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ F\ F')$
is $\top$. Then $\mathrm{genusFF}\ K\ F \le \mathrm{genusFF}\ K'\ F'$, where $\mathrm{genusFF}$ of a
function field is the $K$-dimension of the adelic $H^1$ of the zero divisor.

This is one inequality of the classical invariance of the genus under extension of an algebraically
closed constant field; it is used by
[`AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`]
(thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed),
which combines it with the reverse inequality to identify the two genera.

